-<p class="shesh-desc">layer: alloc Open addressing with linear probing over parallel mala arrays. KEY REPRESENTATION: byte strings (the R10 strb_* surface), NOT char-code arrays: keys are usually literals (&quot;apple&quot;), and byte strings let the caller pass a literal directly. The hash (lib/hash.smlib fnv1a) is byte-based (char_at), so the choice is consistent end to end. Do not pass char-code arrays here. Layout of the map buffer m (qword cells, except the key bytes): m[0]           capacity m[1]           live entry count m[2+i]         state[i]   (0 = empty, 1 = live), i in 0..cap-1 m[2+cap+i]     keylen[i] m[2+2*cap+i]   val[i] key bytes: byte region at byte offset (2+3*cap)*8, KEY_MAX bytes/slot. KEY_MAX = 32: keys longer than 32 bytes are truncated to 32, consistently on put/get/contains/remove (documented; excluded from the properties). cap must be &gt;= 1 (clamped). Probing wraps modulo cap. DELETION is backward-shift (Knuth 6.4R): the freed slot is filled by shifting later probe-chain entries back toward their home bucket, so there is no &quot;deleted&quot; state and no tombstones — a lookup stops at the first empty slot and never misses a live entry. ABSENT SENTINEL: nighantu_grah returns -1 (0-1) for a missing key. Values are programmer-managed integers; do not store -1 as a value unless you disambiguate with nighantu_antah first. FULL TABLE: nighantu_khip returns 0 and changes nothing.</p>
